From: WelsonJS
Subject: [PATCH] STQ1_0 ternary quantization (PR #22836) for this fork

STQ1_0 support: the PR itself, an x86 SIMD kernel, and reading the STQ1_0
files Tencent publishes (tencent/Hy-MT2-1.8B-1.25Bit-GGUF).

1. ggml-cpu : add STQ1_0 ternary quantization with ARM NEON vec_dot kernel

  Source: https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/pull/22836
  PR head: 1e411d8f5a1e23525fa3265dfb4bd76265465397 (open, not merged upstream)
  Rebased onto: the llama.cpp fork used by bitnet.cpp,
    https://github.com/isHuangXin/llama.cpp.git 390c307752ab78fd8189f359d6954c9ba1be74af
    (submodule 3rdparty/llama.cpp of microsoft/BitNet 0b341e582afbf9e1011f24744b554c96a3477eb5).
  Changes from the PR:
    - Type IDs: the fork uses GGML types 36-38 and 42 for I2_S, I8_S, TL1 and
      TL2, and llama file types 41-43 for I2_S, TL1 and TL2; it has neither
      Q2_0 nor F8_E4M3. Those IDs are kept.
      - GGML type: STQ1_0 keeps the PR's ID 43 (GGML_TYPE_COUNT 44).
        Tencent's published STQ1_0 files store type 42 (TL2 here); part 3
        detects them by their tensor sizes.
      - LLAMA_FTYPE: the PR's 42 is LLAMA_FTYPE_MOSTLY_TL1 in the fork (and 43
        is TL2), so LLAMA_FTYPE_MOSTLY_STQ1_0 is 44. The file type is metadata
        only (general.file_type).
    - Context lines adjusted for the fork, which has no Q2_0 entries; the
      STQ1_0 lines follow the TQ2_0 lines instead.
    - ggml/src/ggml-cpu/arch-fallback.h: the fork's x86 section already has an
      empty quants.c block, which receives the STQ1_0 generic mapping.
    - gguf-py/gguf/constants.py: the fork defines LlamaFileType twice (the
      second definition wins); MOSTLY_STQ1_0 is added to both.

2. ggml-cpu : add an x86 SIMD vec_dot for STQ1_0

  STQ1_0 (part 1, PR #22836) has a fast vec_dot only for ARM NEON; on x86
  it runs ggml_vec_dot_stq1_0_q8_K_generic, which decodes one weight at a
  time. tencent/Hy-MT2-1.8B-1.25Bit-GGUF generated about 2 tokens/s with it on
  a 12-core x86 PC, against about 27 tokens/s for the Q4_K_M file of the same
  model.

  Add ggml_vec_dot_stq1_0_q8_K to arch/x86/quants.c for CPUs with SSE4.1 or
  AVX (the sse42, sandybridge and newer variants of GGML_CPU_ALL_VARIANTS;
  GGML_SSE42 is tested because MSVC does not define __SSE4_1__), and drop the
  x86 mapping of the generic function to that name in arch-fallback.h. Other
  x86 CPUs call the generic function as before.

  In each 64-weight chunk, group g (0..15) holds weights g + p*16 (p = 0..3),
  so the kernel builds the 16 five-bit codebook indices of a chunk, looks them
  up with two _mm_shuffle_epi8 (one per codebook half) blended by the sign
  bits, and multiplies each 2-bit field with 16 activations using
  _mm_maddubs_epi16. The codes are 0/1/2 for -1/0/+1, so the sum is
  sum(q * y) - sum(y), with sum(y) from the q8_K bsums. The arithmetic is
  integer, so the result equals the generic function's.

  Measured: 28-30 tokens/s (AVX2 variant), 23-24 (sandybridge), 10 (sse42),
  2 (x64, generic), with the same translations on every variant.

3. gguf : read type-42 tensors as STQ1_0 when their sizes say so

  GGML type 42 has two meanings:

    - GGML_TYPE_TL2 in this fork (bitnet.cpp's lookup-table type), and
    - STQ1_0 in the GGUF files Tencent publishes for it
      (tencent/Hy-MT2-1.8B-1.25Bit-GGUF: 42 bytes per 256 weights).

  This build keeps the fork's TL2 = 42 and numbers STQ1_0 43, as PR #22836
  does, so files that follow either numbering keep working. To also read
  Tencent's files, gguf_init_from_file_impl looks at the tensor offsets, which
  must match the tensor sizes (it already checks that right after): when a file
  has type-42 tensors and the offsets match their sizes as STQ1_0 but not as
  TL2, those tensors are read as STQ1_0. A real TL2 file matches as TL2 and is
  not changed; a file that matches neither fails the existing offset check as
  before.

  general.file_type has the same problem, so the model loader goes by the
  tensor types for two numbers:

    - 41 is LLAMA_FTYPE_MOSTLY_I2_S here and the file type of Tencent's STQ1_0
      files: reported as MOSTLY_STQ1_0 when the file has STQ1_0 tensors and no
      I2_S tensors;
    - 40 is LLAMA_FTYPE_MOSTLY_Q1_0 here and the file type of
      microsoft/BitNet-b1.58-2B-4T-gguf: reported as MOSTLY_I2_S when the file
      has I2_S tensors and no Q1_0 tensors.

  The file type is metadata only.

Apply with: git -c core.autocrlf=false apply <this file>

